error[ffi_call_shape]: `errno.h` declares `errno` as an object of type `int`, not a function: clang read the header, and the call this declaration implies does not fit it
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-152-an-object-never-called.hero:11:5
     |
  11 |     function errno() -> i32  #~ ffi_call_shape
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: an object can hold another value at the next read, so no group member binds one, and a `constant` refuses it (§4.19): a function of the program's own returns it, written in a header beside this file and bound by `extern` naming that header like any function, `static inline int hero_errno(void) { return errno; }`
